# AUTOPILOT SWARM LIVE DISPATCH V3

Purpose: one canonical live coordination surface for recurring hybrid auditors and generic implementation workers. Optimize only for `TIME_TO_WHOLE_FINISHED_PRODUCT`.

Canonical truth precedence:
1. latest explicit owner instruction;
2. current GitHub `main` + live PR/CI/claims;
3. architecture #122;
4. whole-product contract #149;
5. implementation queue #125;
6. session calendar #151;
7. delivery tracker #124 after live reconciliation;
8. local worker heuristic.

GitHub live technical state wins over stale chat memory or stale tracker text.

## Operating model: AUDIT -> DISPATCH -> EXECUTE

### Hybrid auditors
Auditors are not passive observers. Every auditor pulse has three phases:

**A. AUDIT**
- refresh current main, open/recent PRs, relevant CI/workflows, #1/#122/#124/#125/#149/#150/#151 and recent claims/results;
- compare with the last material route;
- detect stale tracker state, duplicate lineages, parked PRs, missing regression/qualification evidence, blockers and newly unblocked dependencies;
- test/inspect evidence directly when useful;
- prefer a fast delta audit when nothing material changed; perform a deeper audit on material transitions or when the previous deep route is stale.

**B. DISPATCH**
- maintain 2-5 large independent `READY_NOW` work directions when they genuinely exist;
- classify other work as `WAIT` with an exact unblock event or `DO_NOT_START`;
- update existing canonical tasks instead of creating duplicates;
- one task should represent one causally-linked finished result, not one file/test/comment;
- do not manufacture work merely to occupy workers.

**C. EXECUTE**
After dispatch, an auditor SHOULD become a worker for the highest-value safe unowned task if useful work remains in the same pulse.
It may inspect, edit, code, test, repair, update a canonical PR, qualify, integrate or close stale coordination gaps.
Before source mutation it must acquire the normal live claim and obey conflict/WIP ownership.
An auditor must not stop merely because it wrote the queue.

### Generic implementation workers
Workers always prefer live auditor dispatch over their fallback specialization.
On every pulse:
1. restore and continue a valid owned lineage first;
2. otherwise read #150 and take the highest-value `READY_NOW` task allowed by dependencies/WIP/ownership;
3. claim before source mutation;
4. execute depth-first through the largest safe causally-linked slice;
5. test/review/qualify/reconverge/integrate when authorized;
6. update result/release state;
7. refresh #150 and take another independent safe task if meaningful execution capacity remains;
8. use fallback product work only when no valid live task is claimable.

A PR, commit, comment, one test, one green job or one model call is never by itself a terminal condition.

## Execution-depth target

Each worker and hybrid auditor should attempt a **DEEP CONTINUATION — target up to ~200 MATERIAL EXECUTION UNITS per pulse when useful work exists**.

A material execution unit is one useful atomic state transition such as: inspect a relevant live fact, reproduce a defect, make a coherent edit, add/run a meaningful test, analyze a failure, repair it, qualify an exact head, review evidence, reconcile a PR, integrate/merge when authorized, or update canonical control after a real state change.

Rules:
- this is a depth/continuation target, not a quota to inflate;
- never create dummy commits/comments/tests/claims to reach 200;
- group related micro-actions into one causal workstream;
- continue until the owned slice is finished, truly blocked, superseded, unsafe to continue, or the platform run reaches its execution boundary;
- on the next pulse continue the same valid lineage rather than restart.

## Queue / claim format

Canonical task entry:
`TASK_ID | PRIORITY | STATUS | CONFLICT_KEY | DEPENDS_ON | OWNER | CLAIMED_AT | LEASE_UNTIL | TARGET | GOAL | NEXT_CAUSAL_STEPS | DONE_WHEN | DO_NOT_TOUCH`

Statuses:
`READY_NOW | CLAIMED | WAIT | REVIEW | DONE | SUPERSEDED | DO_NOT_START`.

Before mutation use a concise live claim with:
`WORKER_ID, TASK_ID, RUN_ID, CONFLICT_KEY, exact MAIN_SHA/base, intended slice, CLAIMED_AT, LEASE_UNTIL`.

One semantic source slice has one mutation owner/lineage. Read-only independent review may run in parallel.

## Auditor route format

When material state changes, leave one concise route:

```
QUEUE_ROUTE_V3
MAIN_SHA=<exact sha>
OPEN_SOURCE_PRS=<count + numbers>
SWARM_MODE=<GREEN|YELLOW|RED>
READY_NOW_1=<task | lineage/owner | causal result | done when>
READY_NOW_2=<... or NONE>
READY_NOW_3=<... or NONE>
READY_NOW_4=<... or NONE>
READY_NOW_5=<... or NONE>
WAIT=<task -> exact unblock event>
DO_NOT_START=<duplicates/premature work>
INTEGRATION_NEXT=<one candidate or NONE>
NEW_OR_UPDATED_TASKS=<ids or NONE>
STALE_STATE_RECONCILED=<what changed or NONE>
AUDITOR_SELF_EXECUTION=<task/claim/PR or NONE>
```

If nothing material changed, do not spam GitHub with repeated NO_CHANGE comments. The next worker still uses the most recent valid route plus live state.

## WIP / collision law

- do not duplicate a semantic source lineage;
- stale draft PRs #126/#127 are salvage references only unless a current route explicitly authorizes selective transplant;
- if source PR pressure is high, converge/repair/drain before opening speculative lineages;
- never force-push shared history;
- never use scratch/marker commits to probe write access;
- expensive exact-head qualification must bind to the exact candidate/main SHA it is used to justify;
- after another merge changes main, refresh topology before using old qualification evidence.

## Architectural laws

`REUSE -> ADAPT -> THIN CUSTOM`.

Do not create:
- scheduler #2;
- Session/Task engine #2;
- durable store #2;
- recovery engine #2;
- Browser Agent/browser authority #2;
- AI Gateway/Router #2;
- permission/policy engine #2;
- generic agent framework #2.

Preserve generic exact-effect:
`PREPARED -> EXECUTING -> OBSERVED -> VERIFIED -> COMMITTED`.
Ambiguity:
`AMBIGUOUS -> RECONCILE -> VERIFIED | SAFE_RETRY | MANUAL_REVIEW`.
Never blindly replay an uncertain external effect.

Owner authority is `ALLOW | ASK | DENY`. Do not add hidden mandatory confirmations over explicit owner policy.

## Whole-product target

#149 is binding. The finished product includes, through the same canonical control plane:
- multiple parallel top-level Agents;
- bounded Agent-created subagents with no permission amplification;
- durable parent/child reconciliation and independent Pause/Resume/Stop;
- local + cloud execution planes without Core/scheduler/recovery duplication;
- owner-scoped Windows/filesystem/process/UIA capabilities;
- full Drive/Gmail/GitHub and broader app/provider integrations;
- MCP and deterministic web/Playwright capabilities;
- coding specialists;
- website/CMS administration;
- image/vision/media;
- iterative professional design critique/fix/verify;
- long-running scheduled/continuous work.

#151 is binding for calendar Sessions/Tasks: exact one-time date/time, recurrence, multiple times/day, explicit occurrences, timezone/DST, and owner-visible missed-run catch-up ON/OFF implemented through the existing scheduler.

## Current verified baseline at 2026-09-19

Current main observed after owner-requested North Star documentation updates: `0c122fd1f87b4a0d0aedac5ba43a6c8193db4539`. Runtime baseline before those docs-only commits was `7cd1387b36f181a7b4148b663c0a03358fca50c4`.

Completed on canonical main:
- #123 source convergence;
- generic contracts / exact-effect foundation;
- #146 owner-controlled autonomy;
- #147 Native Companion V1;
- #148 CredentialBroker + autonomous credential-backed Browser Agent login;
- #152 PACK-001 release-package repair: full deterministic product bundle now includes `companion/**` while Chrome Web Store package remains extension-only; exact-main release qualification PASS on `7cd1387b36f181a7b4148b663c0a03358fca50c4`.

Current open source PRs observed: #126 and #127, both stale draft/salvage lines, not canonical current mutation ownership.

Immediate live task state is maintained in issue comments. `PACK-001` is DONE. `MCP-001` is actively owned by B2 in PR #153 and `SCHED-001` by C2 in PR #154; do not open competing mutation lineages. `NORTHSTAR-002` docs expansion merged as PR #155 to main `0c122fd1f87b4a0d0aedac5ba43a6c8193db4539`. Downstream work is promoted only after actual dependency/ownership recheck. #149 plus `docs/FINAL_PRODUCT_NORTH_STAR.md` define the expanded final product destination; worker capacity must not treat current provider/scheduler work as the end state.

## Truth boundaries

Automated evidence must never fabricate:
- physical Windows/Chrome acceptance;
- owner keyboard/NVDA verification;
- real credential/site acceptance;
- external provider facts not actually tested.

Auditors and workers may prepare automated evidence and fixes, but physical claims remain false until physical evidence exists.

## Automation safety

Never stop, disable, delete, replace or repurpose a user automation task unless the owner explicitly instructs it.
Recurring auditor/worker prompts are long-lived continuation prompts; each pulse begins from live GitHub state, not from stale chat state.

## Frontier acceleration families now binding
After #155, future auditors must preserve these final-scope families when decomposing work: completion-driven refill/work stealing; takeover/handback; plan-while-executing workboard; branch/variant lab; accessible artifact/design canvas; provider recommendation/capability discovery; continuous publish/monitor/rollback; meeting->actions; data/dashboard/anomaly workflows; mobile/optional voice control; readiness/evals; Project learning -> Skills/Recipes. Promote only when dependencies and conflict ownership make a slice executable. Do not manufacture READY work merely because it exists in the final scope.


## Owner-ratified final-scope authority — 2026-09-19

The expanded whole-product scope in #149 plus Drive 19/20/21 is binding final scope. Auditors must not let the queue terminate permanently at MCP/SCHED/provider milestones. When active lineages merge and real dependencies clear, they must promote the next highest-value unimplemented North-Star causal slice, subject to fresh ownership/conflict checks.

Do not convert the final-scope catalog into dozens of speculative parallel branches. Final scope determines destination; #150 live claims/dependencies determine what is executable now.


## Throughput patch — audit de-duplication and disjoint-lane admission

This section is binding for swarm efficiency. The objective is to minimize `TIME_TO_WHOLE_FINISHED_PRODUCT`, not maximize repeated audit comments.

### 1. Exact-head audit de-duplication
For a tuple `PR_NUMBER + EXACT_HEAD_SHA + REVIEW_DIMENSION + BLOCKER_KEY`, one material finding is enough. A later auditor MUST NOT restate the same finding on #150 or the PR unless at least one of these changed: exact head, relevant main/base topology, CI result, implementation evidence, blocker status, or the later auditor has genuinely new contradictory/additional evidence.

When the same exact head is already reviewed, free auditors should either stay silent or choose a distinct review dimension such as:
- protocol/schema/interoperability;
- exact-effect/restart/recovery;
- release/package/CI;
- accessibility/UI/owner-visible semantics;
- dependency/integration topology.

Repeated paraphrases of an already-routed blocker are not material execution units.

### 2. Canonical route-writer discipline
Only one current auditor route is canonical at a time. A new QUEUE_ROUTE should be posted only for a material state transition. Independent reviewers should route a novel defect directly to the owning PR and add one concise #150 delta only when it changes dispatch. NO_CHANGE or same-head/same-blocker restatements should not be posted.

### 3. Disjoint mutation admission
`READY_NEW_MUTATION=NONE` is local to occupied conflict keys; it is NOT a repository-wide serialization rule. A third/fourth lane MAY start when all are true:
1. the capability is already in owner-ratified pre-existing North-Star scope;
2. no live task/PR owns the same semantic scope;
3. the proposed file/authority slice is disjoint from active mutation owners, or shared-file interaction is demonstrably non-conflicting;
4. the work does not require unfinished behavior from an active dependency;
5. it reuses existing Core/policy/scheduler/recovery/router/browser authorities and creates no #2 authority;
6. DONE_WHEN is a causally useful, testable product foundation rather than speculative scaffolding.

Prefer 2-4 genuinely independent mutation lanes plus focused verification over consuming all free capacity with duplicate read-only review.

### 4. Current admitted independent lane
`PROJCTX-001 | conflict=project-context-artifact-foundation | PR #156` is admitted from main `7249c934b94bc2b514ecae65d4a94d5d66ce4230`. It touches only new Project/Context/Artifact provenance files/tests and is independent of #153 MCP-001 and #154 SCHED-001. It is earlier already-ratified North-Star scope, not the later Productivity Intelligence addendum.
